1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,917
Every recorded call is listed on one page, whatever kind of call it was.

2
00:00:05,917 --> 00:00:11,148
This video shows why recordings matter, who sees which calls, which calls are

3
00:00:11,148 --> 00:00:16,380
recorded, how to search them, and what the call page and its transcript show.

4
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:26,063
When a customer says the agent promised something, or an agent needs coaching,

5
00:00:26,063 --> 00:00:29,088
a note written after the call is not enough.

6
00:00:29,088 --> 00:00:30,480
The recording is.

7
00:00:31,230 --> 00:00:36,248
Recordings are personal data, so who may listen has to be controlled, and

8
00:00:36,248 --> 00:00:40,060
one customer's call must never be open to every agent.

9
00:00:40,810 --> 00:00:41,546
An A.I.

10
00:00:41,546 --> 00:00:44,207
voice agent's calls need more than audio.

11
00:00:44,207 --> 00:00:48,510
You want to read what was said, and jump to the moment you care about.

12
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:54,375
The Call recordings page lists every recorded call in one place, with search,

13
00:00:54,375 --> 00:00:59,120
playback, transcripts, and a way to erase a recording when you have to.

14
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:08,189
With the permission Listen to own call recordings, the page lists only the

15
00:01:08,189 --> 00:01:10,258
calls you were the agent on.

16
00:01:10,258 --> 00:01:13,666
You cannot search for, list or open anyone else's.

17
00:01:13,666 --> 00:01:15,370
The Agent role has it.

18
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:21,168
With Listen to anyone's call recordings, the page lists every recorded call, and

19
00:01:21,168 --> 00:01:23,163
you can search by agent too.

20
00:01:23,163 --> 00:01:25,100
The Supervisor role has it.

21
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:33,978
Calls are recorded while the Contact Center Call Recording feature is on, and

22
00:01:33,978 --> 00:01:39,840
Record every call automatically is checked in the Contact Center settings, which it is by default.

23
00:01:40,590 --> 00:01:44,315
A queue call or a dialer call is recorded from the moment it

24
00:01:44,315 --> 00:01:45,839
connects to an agent.

25
00:01:45,839 --> 00:01:46,572
An A.I.

26
00:01:46,572 --> 00:01:50,410
voice agent's call is recorded from the moment it is answered.

27
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:56,481
A number dialed on the soft phone keypad is recorded when the other side answers.

28
00:01:56,481 --> 00:02:00,090
An extension call between colleagues is not recorded.

29
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:04,574
A call shows up on the page once its recording has been saved,

30
00:02:04,574 --> 00:02:07,320
which can take a minute after the call ends.

31
00:02:11,582 --> 00:02:14,498
Open Interaction Center, Call recordings.

32
00:02:14,498 --> 00:02:19,647
The page says that no recorded call matches until a recording has been saved.

33
00:02:19,647 --> 00:02:23,122
Calls are listed here once their recording exists.

34
00:02:23,647 --> 00:02:28,144
Started is the date range to search, such as Today, Last 7 days

35
00:02:28,144 --> 00:02:31,207
or a custom range, in your own time zone.

36
00:02:31,713 --> 00:02:35,313
Phone number matches all or part of the customer's number.

37
00:02:36,054 --> 00:02:38,566
Direction is Inbound or Outbound.

38
00:02:38,566 --> 00:02:41,399
Call type is Contact Center call, A.I.

39
00:02:41,399 --> 00:02:43,974
voice agent, or Soft phone keypad.

40
00:02:44,445 --> 00:02:48,782
Agent picks whose calls to list, from the Contact Center agents.

41
00:02:48,782 --> 00:02:52,625
It is shown only to users who may hear everyone's calls.

42
00:02:53,117 --> 00:02:56,699
Click Filter to search, or Clear to start again.

43
00:02:56,699 --> 00:03:02,338
When calls match, each row shows the customer's number, the direction, the call

44
00:03:02,338 --> 00:03:06,317
type, when the call started, the agent and the length.

45
00:03:10,517 --> 00:03:13,408
Play plays the recording right in the list.

46
00:03:13,408 --> 00:03:15,826
Click it again to close the player.

47
00:03:15,826 --> 00:03:17,949
One recording plays at a time.

48
00:03:17,949 --> 00:03:19,777
View opens the call page.

49
00:03:20,527 --> 00:03:24,126
The call page shows who was on the call and when, a player

50
00:03:24,126 --> 00:03:27,162
for the recording and, below it, the transcript.

51
00:03:27,162 --> 00:03:31,997
A link takes you to the contact's activities when the call belongs to a contact.

52
00:03:32,747 --> 00:03:33,876
Calls an A.I.

53
00:03:33,876 --> 00:03:36,607
voice agent talked on have a transcript.

54
00:03:36,607 --> 00:03:39,397
Calls between people are not transcribed.

55
00:03:40,147 --> 00:03:43,893
Each line shows the time into the recording, a copy button, a play

56
00:03:43,893 --> 00:03:47,899
button that plays from that line, the silence before the line, who said

57
00:03:47,899 --> 00:03:49,356
it, and what was said.

58
00:03:49,356 --> 00:03:51,957
Clicking the time also plays from that line.

59
00:03:52,707 --> 00:03:54,879
The times are close, not exact.

60
00:03:54,879 --> 00:03:55,876
For an A.I.

61
00:03:55,876 --> 00:04:00,278
call that was handed to an agent, the A.I.'s part happened before the

62
00:04:00,278 --> 00:04:05,207
agent's recording started, so those lines show dashes and have no play button.

63
00:04:09,407 --> 00:04:14,267
Only users with the Delete call recordings permission see Erase recording at the

64
00:04:14,267 --> 00:04:15,962
bottom of the call page.

65
00:04:15,962 --> 00:04:18,957
No role has it by default except Administrator.

66
00:04:19,707 --> 00:04:24,389
Type why the recording is being erased, for example because the customer asked

67
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:27,287
for their data to be deleted, and click Erase.

68
00:04:28,037 --> 00:04:31,730
The recording is deleted for good and no longer listed.

69
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:34,877
A recording under legal hold cannot be erased.

70
00:04:39,077 --> 00:04:43,875
A supervisor coaching an agent searches that agent's calls for the week, and

71
00:04:43,875 --> 00:04:45,747
plays a few from the list.

72
00:04:46,497 --> 00:04:51,526
A manager handling a complaint searches by the customer's phone number, finds the

73
00:04:51,526 --> 00:04:54,127
call, and reads the moment in question.

74
00:04:54,877 --> 00:04:56,583
A team reviewing an A.I.

75
00:04:56,583 --> 00:05:01,017
voice agent reads the transcripts, and jumps to where a call went wrong.

76
00:05:01,767 --> 00:05:07,867
A company answering a data deletion request erases the recording, with the reason written on it.

77
00:05:09,867 --> 00:05:15,034
Search the calls, play them back, read the transcript, and erase a recording

78
00:05:15,034 --> 00:05:16,609
only when you must.

79
00:05:16,609 --> 00:05:18,247
Thanks for watching.

